The VerifiedSecurity2 Java adapter is derived from Espressif's Android
provisioning SDK, lib-2.4.4, commit b83b78543fcd7ae24c9acbefdc17cad3ed4a3607:
provisioning/src/main/java/com/espressif/provisioning/security/Security2.java
Copyright 2022 Espressif Systems (Shanghai) PTE LTD, Apache License 2.0.

VerifiedSrpClient is adapted from the same SDK SRP6ClientSession and
ClientSRP6Routines (also copyright Connect2id Ltd. and others, 2011–2019).
It preserves leading zero bytes in salts and SHA-512 outputs, rejects invalid
public values, and compares the server proof in constant time.

Local changes require Security 2 patch 1, reject invalid authentication and
protocol messages, propagate cryptographic failures, use GCMParameterSpec,
and reject AES-GCM counter exhaustion. No ESPDevice security negotiation or
credential logging is used. See LICENSE-ESPRESSIF for the license.
